{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.run_pair_sum_eq_sum_min","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.run_pair_sum_eq_sum_min","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/EdgeDecoupling.lean#L184-L203","doc":"**The run's pair sum, both halves, as one sum over distances.**\n\nThis is the shape `rev_e_infinity_closed_form_probe.py::run_direct` actually computes: each row\nof the run contributes upward to every row above it that lies outside the run, and downward to\nevery row below it that does.  The two conditions are different (`j < d` and `ell ≤ j + d`) and\ncarry different kernels, and the identity is that both collect with the same multiplicity, so\nthe run's whole contribution is a single sum over `d` against the combined kernel\n\n    T d  =  fUp d + fDown d .\n\nAt `fUp d = ε(2d) − ε(2d+1)` and `fDown d = ε(2d) − ε(2d−1)` that combined kernel is exactly the\nprobe's `T(d) = 2ε(2d) − ε(2d−1) − ε(2d+1)`.  Nothing here says that series converges, or what\nits value is; it says the run depends on `ell` only through the weights `min d ell` — which is\nwhy `Xrun` is a function of the run length alone and carries no `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.sum_heads_eq_sum_min","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.sum_heads_eq_sum_min","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/EdgeDecoupling.lean#L176-L182","doc":"**Collecting the run's downward straddling pairs by distance.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.sum_tails_eq_sum_min","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.sum_tails_eq_sum_min","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/EdgeDecoupling.lean#L164-L174","doc":"**Collecting the run's upward straddling pairs by distance.**\n\nThe left side is how the pair sum is generated — row by row of the run, each contributing every\ndistance beyond it.  The right side is how it is evaluated — distance by distance, each with the\nmultiplicity `min d ell`.  They are equal by exchanging the order of summation and counting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.card_filter_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.card_filter_ge","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/EdgeDecoupling.lean#L148-L162","doc":"The rows whose *downward* reach at distance `d` clears the run: also `min d ell`.\n\nThis is the reflection `j ↦ ell - 1 - j` of `card_filter_lt`, and it is not a restatement — the\ndownward half of the run's pair sum is generated by a different condition (`ell ≤ j + d`, the\nrow plus the distance leaving the run at the bottom) and only *lands* on the same count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.card_filter_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.card_filter_lt","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/EdgeDecoupling.lean#L136-L146","doc":"The rows of the run whose *upward* reach at distance `d` clears the run: `min d ell`.\n\nThe `min` is the whole content — a distance shorter than the run is contributed by only the\nfirst `d` rows, a distance longer than it by all `ell`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.cross_sum_le_geom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.cross_sum_le_geom","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/EdgeDecoupling.lean#L100-L114","doc":"**The decoupling, in the form the `REV_n` arc uses it.** A kernel dominated by a geometric\n`C rᴹ` makes the cross term `O(rᴿ)` in the separation `R`, so two groups of rows that move apart\nstop interacting geometrically fast.\n\n`ε(m) = −log(1 − q₀^{−2m}) ≤ q₀^{−2m} / (1 − q₀^{−2})` is such a kernel with `r = q₀^{−2} < 1`,\nwhich is why the three pieces of the maximiser separate at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.cross_sum_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.cross_sum_le","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/EdgeDecoupling.lean#L82-L98","doc":"**The decoupling estimate.** If the kernel `g` is antitone and every member of `A` is at\nleast `R` away from every member of `B`, then the cross term is at most `|A| · |B| · g R`.\n\nStated with `•` rather than `*` so it needs only an ordered `AddCommMonoid`: the multiplication\nby two cardinalities is repeated addition, not ring multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.cross_sum_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.cross_sum_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/EdgeDecoupling.lean#L75-L80","doc":"A non-negative kernel gives a non-negative cross term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.sum_pairs_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EdgeDecoupling.sum_pairs_split","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/EdgeDecoupling.lean#L56-L73","doc":"A double sum over one index set splits, over any decidable predicate `P`, into the two\nwithin-class sums and the two cross sums.\n\nThis is the exact statement that \"restrict the displacement to one group\" is a summand: no\norder, no metric, no decay — it holds in any `AddCommMonoid`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}